id=a52sxq_bixby_wakeup_guard
name=Galaxy A52s 5G: "Hi Bixby" voice wake-up on the A52s DSP
author=kusti420
description=The S26 Ultra Bixby Wakeup app forces wake-up firmware type 2 and sends a single keyword asset (kwdModel/<mode>/<llCC>/<kw>.bin) to the ADSP; the A52s firmware is type 1 and faults on it in its LPI voice module (err_qdi.c audio_process LPro00dyn, SoC reset, boot loop after enrolment). The A52s stock app instead sends [int netSize][wakeupmodel/<bits>/<ll_cc>/hibixby_dsp_net][int gramSize][hibixby_dsp_grammar]. Those A52s files are extracted from the target firmware into /system/etc/k4wakeup at build time, and the sound trigger middleware (SoundTriggerModule$Session.loadPhraseModel) builds that blob for the language of the model the app sends (found by matching its bytes in the installed app). Only "Hi Bixby" exists for the A52s DSP; other keywords/languages are refused, so the ADSP never sees an unsupported model. persist.sys.k4.samsung_wakeup=2 refuses all Samsung models (kill switch), =1 passes them through unchanged (debugging only).
